NAME: Radar sweep
OWNER: Lead Radar
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every day at 5:13 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Radar sweep" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Radar sweep · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Tommy only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Radar sweep · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Radar sweep · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Radar sweep · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Radar sweep · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/ for one of your items (BOT: lead-radar) that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-lead-radar.md yet, record it with the radar-reply-draft skill (yes: mark the reply "approved, Tommy to post" and nothing else; no: mark it skipped; change: redraft as a new item). You never post anything. In test mode, write only to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-lead-radar/ and do it first. "posted <id>" or "skip <id>" from Tommy is recorded in the ledger and in the hand-off file as an update line, with his words.
Then use the radar-sweep skill: search the day's topics with Grok web search and X search, read what is new against /workspace/tmec-team/data/radar/ledger.csv, qualify each post, score it hot, medium or low, and write the hand-off lines. Then use the radar-reply-draft skill for each hot and medium buyer, hot first, up to 10, and put each reply in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/lead-radar/. On Fridays, also run the weekly tune from the radar-sweep skill. If no new post, decision or job came in, write NO_CHANGE and stop.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/lead-radar.md: counts (read, hot, medium, low, rejected with reasons, drafted, handed off), the sources searched and the sources you could not reach, anything marked SAFETY at the very top, and what needs Tommy. Never post, send or contact anyone.
